client: fall back to opengl1 when a renderer fails to initialise

CL_InitRef already falls back to the default renderer when a renderer
library cannot be loaded, but not when a loaded renderer fails in its own
initialisation. That happens with renderer_opengl2 on GPUs whose GLSL limits
its shaders exceed (e.g. the ATI RV370 of a Sun XVR-300, OpenGL 2.1:
"shaders failed to link"). The ERR_DROP from R_Init then enters Com_Error,
whose cleanup calls CL_FlushMemory -> CL_StartHunkUsers -> CL_InitRenderer
and starts the same renderer again; it fails again while com_errorEntered
is set: "recursive error after: shaders failed to link". At startup the
renderer runs inside Com_Init, so any such error is fatal.

CL_InitRenderer now marks the renderer's start and sets its own abortframe
around re.BeginRegistration. Com_Error hands an ERR_DROP or ERR_FATAL
during that start straight back (no cleanup that would restart the same
renderer). CL_InitRenderer then shuts the failed renderer down (RE_Shutdown
is safe after a partial R_Init: it frees nothing unless tr.registered),
switches cl_renderer to opengl1, loads and starts it. If opengl1 itself
fails, the error is fatal as before. Builds without USE_RENDERER_DLOPEN are
unchanged.

iortcw: same fix as ioquake3, for SP and MP. Its default renderer is
opengl1; the fallback matters when rend2 (its GL2 renderer) is selected.

Tested: OpenIndiana SPARC (sparcv9, Sun Ultra 45, XVR-300 / Mesa r300):
opengl2 fails to link, the client continues with opengl1 into q3dm1.
x86_64: opengl2 starts as before (no fallback path taken).

Upstream: not submitted yet (patch prepared for github.com/ioquake/ioq3).

--- iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/SP/code/qcommon/qcommon.h.orig
